    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26757" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διηγ-έομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>set out in detail, describe,</i> [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔργα</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Heraclit.
				1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρᾶγμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					198
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἀλήθειαν περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					1.13
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.54
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				310a
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ ταύτης εἰπεῖν καὶ διηγήσασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					21.77
				</span></i>
			: c. acc. pers., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷον . . σὺ τοῦτον
				διηγῇ</span> such as you <i>describe</i> him, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				144c
			</span></i>.</div>
